task (completed) {
  currently when asking a question, the iterative evidence approach is very slow, please find ways to make it faster

  Optimizations implemented                                                                                                                          
  app/chat_server.py                                                                                                                                 
  - Eliminated repeated query expansion — the question is expanded once per loop instead of once per round; missing terms are appended directly to   
  the BM25 query.                                                                                                                                  
  - Stopped duplicate relevance filtering — with an active soft tag, the final tag_filter_candidates already filters for question + tag relevance,   
  so the per-round filter_candidates call was removed. It still runs once for non-tag scopes (/transcript, /article).                              
  - Wider first retrieval batch — round 1 now gathers 2× the normal batch, so most questions finish after one sufficiency check instead of 2–3.      
  - Fewer rounds/checks — non-enumerative cap reduced 4→3, enumerative 6→5; enumerative questions check sufficiency every other round instead of     
  every round.                                                                                                                                     
  - Early stop on unchanged missing terms — avoids a pointless extra round when the checker keeps reporting the same gap.                            
  - Fixed a hidden model-reload penalty — the article router used num_ctx=4096 while all other small-model calls used 8192. Switching context size   
  caused Ollama to reload qwen3:1.7b between calls. All small-model calls now use 8192, avoiding ~1s reloads.                                      
  - Reduced sufficiency output budget 96→64 tokens.                                                                                                  

  chat.py                                                                                                                                            
  - Added an LRU cache for expand_query, shared by the iterative loop, tag routing, and normal retrieval.                                            
  Measured effect                                                                                                                                    

  Warm-model benchmark over the real tag corpus (_youtube_iterative_evidence, tag japan):                                                            

  ┌────────────────────────────────────────┬──────────┬───────┐                                                                                      
  │ Question                               │ Before   │ After │                                                                                      
  ├────────────────────────────────────────┼──────────┼───────┤                                                                                      
  │ where can i get IDP?                   │ 6.5–8.2s │ 3.4s  │                                                                                      
  ├────────────────────────────────────────┼──────────┼───────┤                                                                                      
  │ what are all levels of wagyu           │ 7.3s     │ 4.4s  │                                                                                      
  ├────────────────────────────────────────┼──────────┼───────┤                                                                                      
  │ where is nijo market                   │ 6.6s     │ 3.6s  │                                                                                      
  ├────────────────────────────────────────┼──────────┼───────┤                                                                                      
  │ requirements for 90-day long-stay visa │ 7.5s     │ 5.6s  │                                                                                      
  └────────────────────────────────────────┴──────────┴───────┘                                                                                      

  Roughly 35–50% faster, with fewer small-model calls per question. The task is marked (completed) in prompts/tags.prompt, and no incomplete prompt  
  tasks remain.      
}

