task.research_tags_refactor (completed) {
  research only, save the result result to {directory_of_this_prompt}/research/tags_system_refactor.html {
    - currently, the /tag command relies on a physical tag files that aggregate list of youtube video ids in each file, this makes the video learning process too long
    - for each video, we should still get its transcript, rewrite it and create trunks, but we should not need to bind it to any tags yet
    - instead, when the command /tag <tag_name> is run, we should set a global context of <tag_name, for the <questoin>, we should then only fetch related trunks related to this global context "and" the <question>, this way, each tag is a "soft" tag instead of a "hard" tag
    - also, we should not need a dedicated tag generation process like: youtube_video_tag_gen.py
    - currently, we have a file tag_description.json, where we define list of tags and its description
    we should keep that, but rename the file to tags.json
    if a specific tag is not defined in tags.json, we should consider it is an invalid tag
    - we should also consider using the tag desription in the global tag specific context
  }
}
